From 44bd947b1a2b4043744e0688cde6a90d8762ebb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Daniel <markdanielphd@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 14:41:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: broaden and shell-harden the OpenClaw dist integrity
 check

Testing the check against synthetic trees showed two gaps.

The regex only matched `from "./chunk.js"` with double quotes, so it
would certify a tree as healthy while a bare side-effect import,
`export * from`, or a dynamic import() pointed at a missing chunk. A
check that misses a corruption form is worse than no check.

Writing the single-quote alternative literally also broke the enclosing
shell single-quoted argument. It is now \x27, so the emitted script
contains no literal single quote.

Verified by extracting the exact PHP-produced command from source and
running it against intact and corrupt trees covering all four import
forms: passes clean, and reports each missing target.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 app/Services/ChatGPTAuthService.php | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/Services/ChatGPTAuthService.php b/app/Services/ChatGPTAuthService.php
index a13bd10..f3603c8 100644
--- a/app/Services/ChatGPTAuthService.php
+++ b/app/Services/ChatGPTAuthService.php
@@ -273,15 +273,24 @@ private function extractOauthProfile(string $listJson): ?array
      * succeeds in that state, so version alone is not evidence of a usable
      * install. Exits non-zero if any relative import target is missing.
      */
+    // The regex covers every form a bundler emits a local chunk reference in:
+    // `import x from`, bare side-effect `import`, `export * from`, and dynamic
+    // `import(...)`, in either quote style. A check that misses a corruption
+    // form is worse than no check, since it certifies a broken tree as healthy.
+    //
+    // Quote handling matters: the script is wrapped in shell single quotes, so
+    // it must contain no literal single quote. The single-quote alternative in
+    // the character class is written as \x27 for that reason. Verified against
+    // synthetic intact and corrupt trees covering all four import forms.
     public const DIST_INTEGRITY_CHECK = 'node -e '
         .'\'const fs=require("fs"),d="/usr/lib/node_modules/openclaw/dist";'
         .'if(!fs.existsSync(d))process.exit(1);'
         .'const bad=[];'
         .'for(const f of fs.readdirSync(d).filter(n=>n.endsWith(".js"))){'
         .'const s=fs.readFileSync(d+"/"+f,"utf8");'
-        .'for(const m of s.matchAll(/from\\s*"\\.\\/([A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.js)"/g))'
+        .'for(const m of s.matchAll(/(?:from|import)\\s*\\(?\\s*["\\x27]\\.\\/([A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.js)["\\x27]/g))'
         .'if(!fs.existsSync(d+"/"+m[1]))bad.push(f+" -> "+m[1]);}'
-        .'if(bad.length){console.error("openclaw dist incomplete: "+bad.slice(0,5).join(", "));process.exit(1);}'
+        .'if(bad.length){console.error("openclaw dist incomplete: "+bad.slice(0,8).join(", "));process.exit(1);}'
         .'console.log("openclaw dist ok");\'';
 
     private function openclawDistIsIntact(): bool
